        "deathNote": false,
        "description": {
          "gm": "",
          "value": "<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The Coalescence rolls for Initiative, Ashgut uses Landwaster, Ashgut or Fjordcarver dies, or the Coalescence uses Draconic Resonance or Slam Dunk.</p><hr /><p>Absorbing the opposing magical energies of both Ashgut and Fjordcarver, the polarity of the Coalescence is inverted.</p><p>The attunement of the Coalescence changes (Or is set to a value of its choice if this ability is triggered by rolling Initiative), and it teleports to the middle of the arena, 35 feet away from the dragon it attuned itself to (As long as neither Ashgut nor Fjordcarver move, this places the Coalescence at the center of the arena, on the side of the respective dragon).</p><p>The Coalescence is then immune to all effects of Elemental Attunement until the start of its next turn.</p><p>Whenever Elemental Attunement triggers, the Coalescence should be described as changing its looks to match the dragon it attuned itself to.</p><p><strong>Special</strong> When Ashgut or Fjordcarver dies, the Coalescence permantly sets its attumenent to whichever dragon is still alive, and Landwaster no longer triggers Elemental Attunement.</p>"
        },
